From 6c8d8545ffe8a03ef295fa7ba5518a3fbe67fe23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 18:32:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add CMS, Operations OS, CRM & Quote enhancements with
 security, monitoring, and RLS hardening

### Motivation
- Add an SEO-driven CMS and public growth pages plus product detail pages to support organic acquisition.
- Expand CRM workflows with an operations console, pipeline Kanban, activity timeline, and improved quote lifecycle.
- Harden public and admin APIs with input validation, rate limiting, CAPTCHA, origin checks, and structured error handling.
- Introduce observability hooks and structured logging for production monitoring and incident visibility.

### Description
- Added CMS and marketing site features including blog, case studies, industries, product detail pages, sitemap/robots updates, `SiteHeader` changes, and `components` for CMS management, pipeline board, operations console, and product grid.
- Implemented many server APIs and handlers (`/api/cms/*`, `/api/operations`, `/api/quotes/*`, `/api/advisor`, quote send, quote items, lead updates) and centralized API helpers in `lib/api.ts`, plus supporting libraries for CAPTCHA (`lib/captcha.ts`), rate limiting (`lib/rate-limit.ts`), monitoring (`lib/monitoring.ts`), logging (`lib/logger.ts`), env validation (`lib/env.ts`), pricing configuration, and PDF generation (`lib/quote-pdf.ts`).
- Expanded Supabase schema and policies in `supabase/schema.sql` (CMS tables, personalization/packaging/pricing, production/fulfillment tables, RLS functions/policies, integrity constraints, indices) and added server/admin Supabase client helpers and middleware role checks.
- UX and form updates: quote builder now supports packaging/personalization/pricing rules, quote form integrates Cloudflare Turnstile, and admin flows include CMS manager, send-quote UI, and improved lead/quote pages; plus `env.example`, `next.config.ts`, and dependency upgrades and eslint config.

### Testing
- Ran linting with `npm run lint` and it completed successfully.
- Ran type checking with `npm run typecheck` and it completed successfully.
- No automated unit tests were added in this change set.
